Short answer: Yes. On NeoForge 21.1.x you can keep one generic extract fluid and store all variant metadata (strain id(s), name, color, THC, CBD, effects and extra effects) on the FluidStack tag. GUIs, tanks and your custom items can render/read that data. World placement and vanilla buckets cannot vary by NBT, so keep this fluid tank/pipes only and use a custom “vial/bottle” item with a renderer to show the dynamic color/name.

Key points:
- Encode variant id(s), color, THC, CBD, and a list of effects on the FluidStack tag.
- Mixing: weighted‑average THC/CBD and color; merge variant lists; combine effects by id (max amplifier, sum durations).
- Use your existing `ModDataComponentTypes` on items; mirror the same fields onto the FluidStack tag for consistency.
- Provide a custom item (vial) that stores a FluidStack and a BEWLR‑based renderer to tint/overlay the fluid in the item model.

Below are minimal helpers and a sample vial item + renderer.

